title: Prices, looked up 2026-11-15.
pid: e2c0b9c1-7f3e-4871-92a2-f01b2d3f2525
body: |2-
  Monthly figures are 730 hours of the hourly price. Hetzner's are
  without VAT, Contabo's with it.
  | Machine                               | vCPU / RAM / disk       | Monthly                                       | Includes                                                   | Leaves out                                                        |
  |---------------------------------------+-------------------------+-----------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | Hetzner CPX32, Helsinki (shared AMD)  | 4 / 8 GB / 160 GB       | €30.49, about $34 (Germany €35.99)            | IPv4, 20 TB traffic, billed by the hour, never above this per month | VAT                                                               |
  | Hetzner CPX31, Oregon or Virginia     | 4 / 8 GB / 160 GB       | €62.99, about $70                             | IPv4, 3 TB traffic                                         | VAT                                                               |
  | Contabo Cloud VPS 6                   | 6 / 12 GB / 100 GB NVMe | €7.50, about $8 (€6.00 without VAT)           | IPv4, traffic under a fair-use policy                      | the price needs a 24-month term; cores shared, speed unmeasured   |
  | DigitalOcean Basic                    | 4 / 8 GB / 160 GB       | $48                                           | IPv4, 5 TB traffic                                         |                                                                   |
  | EC2 t4g.large (ARM, burstable)        | 2 / 8 GB                | $49; $31 with a 1-year reservation; ~$20 spot | the machine only                                           | disk at $0.08 per GB (80 GB: $6.40), IPv4 $3.65, outbound traffic |
  | EC2 c7i.xlarge (from your table)      | 4 / 8 GB                | $130                                          | the machine only                                           | the same                                                          |
  Spot machines can be taken back at any time, so they suit only a
  burst, not a desk. Sources: the providers' own price pages for
  Hetzner, Contabo and DigitalOcean; instances.vantage.sh for EC2's
  hourly prices.
